


<exercise>
<introduction>
<p>
Identify the exponent and the coefficient of each power function.
</p>
</introduction>


<task workspace="1in">
<statement>
<p>
<m>y=2x^2\cdot4x^3</m>
</p>
</statement>
<solution>
<p>
Simplifying we get <m>y=8 x^{2+3} = 8x^5</m>. So the exponent is <m>5</m> and the coefficient is <m>8</m>.
</p>
</solution>
</task>


<task workspace="1in">
<statement>
<p>
<m>y=(x^2)^3</m>
</p>
</statement>
<solution>
<p>
Simplifying we get <m>y=x^{2\cdot 3} = x^6</m>. So the exponent is <m>6</m> and the coefficient is <m>1</m>.
</p>
</solution>
</task>


<task workspace="1in">
<statement>
<p>
<m>y=\dfrac{x^8}{7x^3}</m>
</p>
</statement>
<solution>
<p>
Simplifying we get <m>y=\dfrac{x^{8-3}}{7} = \dfrac{x^5}{7}</m> which we can write as <m>y=\frac{1}{7}x^5</m>. Therefore the coefficient is <m>\frac{1}{7}</m> and the exponent is <m>5</m>.
</p>
</solution>
</task>


<task workspace="1in">
<statement>
<p>
<m>y=(0.1x^2)^5(-4x)^2</m>
</p>
</statement>
<solution>

<p>
<md>
<mrow>y \amp \quad = \quad (0.1)^5 (x^2)^5 (-4)^2 (x)^2</mrow>
<mrow>\amp \quad = \quad 0.00001 \,x^{10} (16) x^2</mrow>
<mrow>\amp \quad = \quad 0.00016 \,x^{10+2}</mrow>
<mrow>\amp \quad = \quad 0.00016 \,x^{12}</mrow>
</md>
</p>
<p>
Therefore the coefficient is <m>0.00016</m> and the exponent is <m>12</m>.
</p>
</solution>
</task>


<task workspace="1in">
<statement>
<p>
<m>y=\pbr{\dfrac{(2x)^4}{x^3}}^2</m>
</p>
</statement>
<solution>

<p>
<md>
<mrow>y\amp \quad = \quad \pbr{\frac{16 x^4}{x^3} } ^2</mrow>
<mrow>\amp \quad = \quad \pbr{16 x^{4-3}} ^2</mrow>
<mrow>\amp \quad = \quad \pbr{16x} ^2</mrow>
<mrow>\amp \quad = \quad 16^2 \cdot x^2</mrow>
<mrow>\amp \quad = \quad 256 \cdot x^2</mrow>
</md>
</p>
<p>
Therefore the coefficient is <m>256</m> and the exponent is <m>2</m>.
</p>
</solution>
</task>


<task workspace="1in">
<statement>
<p>
<m>y=\dfrac{8x}{\pi^2}</m>
</p>
</statement>
<solution>
<p>
Here, <m>y=\dfrac{8}{\pi ^2} \cdot x</m> and so the coefficient is <m>\dfrac{8}{\pi ^2}</m> and the exponent is <m>1</m>.
</p>
</solution>
</task>



</exercise>



<exercise>
<introduction>
<p>
Draw a rough sketch of the graph of a power function <m>y=kx^p</m> with the stated properties.
</p>
</introduction>

<task workspace="1in">
<statement>
<p>
negative coefficient and an exponent of 3
</p>
</statement>

<solution>

\begin{tikzpicture}[scale=0.7]
\begin{axis}[grid=none,
axis lines=middle,
axis line style=very thick,
xmin=-2,xmax=2,
ymin=-2,ymax=2,
xtick=\empty,
ytick=\empty,
minor tick={},
xlabel=\(x\), ylabel=\(y\),
samples=250]
\addplot[domain=-2:2 ,thick] {-x^3};
\end{axis}
\end{tikzpicture}

</solution>
</task>



